      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: SHAY DVORETZKY, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners. EPHRAIM MCDOWELL, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:44 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress enacted Section 7609 to give the public critical privacy rights to notice and an opportunity to quash third-party IRS summonses. Congress carefully limited the exceptions to those rights. In clause (1), Congress allowed the IRS to forgo notice for a summons issued \"in aid of the collection of an assessment ... against the person with respect to whose liability the summons is issued.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You said that the IRS is not reading the entire -- entirety of the clauses. Would you tell us exactly what you're relying on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: There has to be some causal link, some close connection of some kind between the liability and -- and --and the IRS's actions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: I didn't hear them as suggesting that the entirety of that -- the subsection didn't apply in the law firm situation, so I'm a little curious about the argument that you just made."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McDowell",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MCDOWELL: Well, first of all, we disagree with the scope of that summons, but -- the characterization of that scope of that summons, as I mentioned --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McDowell",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MCDOWELL: I think, in an ordinary case, that would be out. But I think this could be a different type of case if you think about the facts here, which were they first asked the law firm for the records of Mr. Polselli's payments to the law firm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: What do we do with your friend's argument on the other side that -- the government's reading of the statute renders subsection (ii), if not entirely superfluous, almost so?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Except don't you have a regulation that says you won't engage (2) until there is collection?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1599",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c05bb2b17b6cf0f27e8880766a1511340c32b0cd7e56b536f2681ba5fc847b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c05bb2b17b6-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
